window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: Eavesdropping","paragraphs":["\"Nah, Noah wouldn’t do that.\" Leonard spoke up for him. \"No matter how playful he can be, flirting with a woman old enough to be his mother isn’t something he’d do.\"","Noah immediately nodded. \"Exactly! How could I ever do something like that?\"","Lyria also nodded in agreement. \"I think so too. No matter how much of a tease Noah may be, I don’t think he would ever do something like that to an older woman.\"","Noah felt a little relieved hearing Lyria defend him. ’At least Lyria believes in me.’","Arisha, however, remained unconvinced.","She narrowed her yellow eyes at him for another moment before eventually returning her attention to her food.","\"Well, whatever. I still think you did something, but I’ll let it go.\"","She shrugged indifferently. \"It’s not my problem, anyway.\"","Noah felt a strange bitterness at her words. ’Why does it feel like she’s already decided I’m guilty?’","Still, there was no point in continuing the conversation. He quickly decided to change the subject.","\"So, what’s going to be different during our second semester?\"","\"No idea,\" Damien replied. \"Classes begin tomorrow, so I guess we’ll find out.\"","Draven immediately let out a heavy sigh. \"Ugh... boring classes. Lectures...\"","He looked thoroughly displeased.","Draven clearly preferred practical lessons where he could train, fight, and actually use his strength rather than sit through hours of lectures.","\"I understand you, brother.\"","Ragnar nodded seriously. The two of them clearly shared the same hatred for studying.","The group continued chatting while finishing their lunch, enjoying their first reunion after Noah’s long absence.","---","Later, Noah parted ways with his friends.","He had no particular plans for the rest of the afternoon, so he decided to return to his dormitory and rest for a while.","He had barely walked halfway there when he noticed someone familiar in the distance.","A young man with black hair was walking ahead of him.","Ken Takeane was also from the Raigamine Duchy, the Eastern Duchy where Akari came from.","He and Noah were classmates, and they had fought alongside each other during several practical exercises before.","Since they already knew each other, Noah decided to greet him. But before Noah could call out to him, Ken suddenly turned onto another path.","Noah stopped.","’...Huh?’","Ken was heading toward the back of the dormitory building.","That was the same area where Noah had previously made a deal with Travis and the others before their VR match.","’Why is he going there?’","Noah frowned. Something about Ken’s behavior felt strange. He glanced around before quietly moving toward the large bushes lining both sides of the path.","He crouched behind them and waited.","Ken continued walking. After a short distance, he suddenly stopped. Then he slowly turned around.","His eyes swept across the surroundings. He carefully checked the area, making sure no one was following him.","Noah remained completely still.","’He’s checking whether someone is watching him... good thing I hide, after all no one goes to that place...’","Ken seemed satisfied that he was alone and continued toward the back of the dormitory.","Noah narrowed his eyes. ’Something’s definitely wrong.’","He hadn’t remembered Ken being particularly suspicious before. In fact, Ken had fought alongside them during their practical examination against the demons.","’Does he have some kind of important role in the game?’","The thought immediately crossed Noah’s mind. His curiosity won. He decided to follow him.","Noah quietly made his way around the dormitory and reached the rear compound wall.","He carefully hid behind it and peeked around the corner.","Ken was there. But he wasn’t alone.","Another person was standing with him.","Noah recognized her almost immediately.","\"You finally came back.\"","A familiar female voice reached his ears.","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","’Marina Lumineth.’","It was the elf girl who had been part of Noah’s group during the Oakhaven field trip, when they had gone into the wilderness to hunt monsters.","Marina looked relieved to see Ken.","\"Sigh... So, how did things go?\"","\"Better than expected.\"","Ken reached into his belongings.","\"Take this.\"","Noah remained hidden behind the wall. He couldn’t see what Ken had handed her.","Marina stared at the object in her hands. \"Th-This is really an Everbloom Draught?!\"","Her voice trembled with disbelief. \"You actually found one?! How?\"","\"Don’t ask.\" Ken let out a tired sigh. \"I went through a lot of trouble to get it during the vacation.\"","Despite his exhausted tone, Noah could hear a faint hint of satisfaction in his voice.","Marina stared at the potion as though it were a priceless treasure.","\"With this...\" Her voice suddenly became emotional. \"With this, my sister can be cured.\"","\"Huh?!\"","Ken’s voice suddenly became flustered. \"Wait, Marina! Why are you hugging me?!\"","\"Thank you... Thank you, Ken!\"","Marina’s voice trembled as she hugged him tightly.","\"Because of you, my sister can run around again!\"","It sounded as though she was crying.","Noah remained hidden behind the wall.","’Ah... I get it.’","Everything seemed to make sense now.","’Marina must have a younger sister suffering from some kind of illness that can be treated with a rare potion. Ken went through all that trouble to obtain the Everbloom Draught for her.’","Noah nodded to himself.","’That’s why she’s so emotional.’","However something still didn’t feel right. He continued listening.","\"Thank you...\"","Marina’s voice became quieter.","\"I’ll do whatever you want.\"","\"Sure.\"","Ken’s response was calm.","\"But first, give the potion to your sister. Once she’s actually cured, then you can help me.\"","\"Yes.\"","Marina hesitated before continuing.","\"But... to be honest, it’s not going to be easy to arrange a meeting between you and the Elven Queen.\"","Noah’s expression immediately changed.","’...What?’","\"She’s like an elder sister to me,\" Marina continued.","\"And my family is one of the most loyal houses to the royal family. But even so, I can’t guarantee that Her Majesty will agree to meet you.\"","\"Just try.\"","Ken’s voice became serious.","\"You’re the only hope I have.\"","Marina fell silent for a moment.","\"But why do you want to meet Her Majesty?\"","\"It’s something important.\"","Ken’s voice became guarded.","\"I can’t tell you right now.\"","He paused. \"And as a commoner, I have no way of contacting her directly.\"","Noah remained completely silent behind the wall.","His expression gradually became more serious.","’Okay...’","He had initially thought this was simply a matter of Marina’s sister being sick.","But now. ’This is weird.’","Ken had gone through considerable trouble to obtain an extremely rare potion for Marina.","In exchange, he wanted her help arranging a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And whatever he wanted to discuss with her was apparently important enough that he refused to tell Marina about it.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","’I have no idea what’s going on...’","His curiosity grew stronger.","’And what exactly does Ken Takeane want with the Elven Queen? Does he know about something? or does he have future knowledge? Damn what a coincident I found myself into!!’","---","IMPORTANT RANTT OF AUTHOR!!","[A/N: Hello, guys! This is for all the readers who are still sticking with my novel. I genuinely thank you all from the bottom of my heart. If you’re still reading at this point, that means we probably share a similar taste in stories and novels, haha!","Well, I know my last arc involving Akari might have been pretty bad since I stretched it out for quite a while. I apologize for that. I also know that some of you might not like the idea of her joining the harem.","But honestly, I had already decided this a long time ago. So, if you’re still reading, I guess that means you don’t mind it too much. This novel was always meant to be a harem novel, since, well... I’m a harem novel reader myself, haha! Personally, I don’t really like small harems with only two or three girls I’d rather just write a novel with a single FL. Still I’ve decided to limit the harem to five girls for this novel.","Sigh... Anyway, to those of you who are disappointed or sad about this development, I’m sorry. But at the end of the day, I’m writing the story I personally enjoy. If you like this kind of story, I hope you’ll continue reading and enjoying it. And if it’s not your cup of tea, I won’t force you to keep reading.","As for why I’m saying all this... Well, sometimes we authors also feel down and start questioning whether we should continue writing a book or not. So, I just wanted to share a little bit of what was on my mind. Thank you again to everyone who has stayed with the novel this far. I really appreciate you all! ]"]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Browsing Information [1]","paragraphs":["\"Well, let’s meet again later. I’m exhausted and need to get some rest.\"","Ken’s voice reached Noah from the other side of the wall.","’They’re leaving!’","Noah immediately stopped listening. He didn’t want to risk being discovered.","\"Yes, of course. Let’s go.\"","The two of them began walking.","Noah carefully slipped away from the area.","He moved through the bushes without making a sound and only relaxed once he had reached a considerable distance from the dormitory.","He finally let out a quiet breath.","\"Okay...\"","Noah rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","\"Ken is definitely hiding something.\"","He hadn’t known Ken particularly well before, but what he had witnessed today was enough to make him suspicious.","Ken had secretly met Marina behind the dormitory, handed her an extremely rare potion, and in exchange, asked her to arrange a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And whatever he wanted to discuss with the queen was apparently so important that he wasn’t even willing to tell Marina about it.","Noah thought about it for a moment.","’He gave Marina that Everbloom Draught...’","His eyes narrowed.","’What exactly does that potion do?’","If it was valuable enough for Ken to go through considerable trouble to obtain it during his vacation, there had to be more to it.","’I should find out.’","Noah decided to return to his dormitory.","’I can search for information about it on the internet. There should be something about a potion that rare.’","Back inside his dormitory, Noah lay comfortably on his bed with his phone in hand.","Nancy was curled up beside him, peacefully sleeping.","Noah, however, was far too curious to rest. He opened his browser and began searching. He was lucky that the information about this potion existed there, not hidden like some ancient treasure.","\"Everbloom Draught...\"","He scrolled through one page after another.","The potion was more known to world that he thought. No wonder it’s information existed online.","There were articles about rare potions, alchemical records, medical references, historical documents, and discussions written by adventurers and scholars.","Noah continued reading.","\"Hmm...\"","His expression gradually became more serious.","\"It’s really rare...\"","According to several sources, the Everbloom Draught was an exceptionally difficult potion to produce. Even among high-level healing potions, it was considered a precious item because of the number of severe conditions it could treat.","Noah continued scrolling.","\"It can cure several dangerous diseases...\"","He paused.","\"But which one is considered the most dangerous?\"","His eyes moved down the page. Then he stopped. \"Bloodmoon Rot...\"","The name immediately caught his attention.","Noah clicked on the article and began reading carefully.","Bloodmoon Rot was one of the rarest blood-related disease that gradually corrupted the victim’s bloodstream.","As the disease progressed, crimson-colored veins would begin spreading across the victim’s body. The victim would experience an intense and unnatural thirst, recurring high fever, severe weakness, and eventually the failure of vital organs.","Ordinary medicine and conventional antidotes were completely ineffective against it.","Once the disease reached an advanced stage, death was almost inevitable.","Then Noah noticed the treatment.","Treatment: Everbloom Draught","The potion could completely purify the corrupted blood and eliminate the disease from the victim’s body.","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","\"This is...\"","He continued reading.","Then he reached the section describing the origin of the disease.","Known Cause: Vampires.","According to historical and medical records, certain highborn vampires from House Bloodwyn possessed a rare ability to infect their enemies with Bloodmoon Rot. Rather than killing their victims immediately, they could cause their blood to slowly deteriorate, allowing the disease to consume the victim over time.","Noah stared at the screen.","His expression slowly changed.","’Vampires...’","That single word caught his attention far more than anything else on the page.","’If Marina’s sister has this disease...’","His thoughts began connecting the pieces.","’That would mean she was infected by a highborn vampire.’","Noah frowned.","’But that doesn’t make sense.’","Vampires had been extinct for a century. At least, that was what history claimed.","Noah changed the tab of his browser and search for history about vampires. He does know few things from old Noah’s memory. Still he decided to read it again.","The Kingdom of Vespermark had once existed on an island near the Demon Continent.","It had been a small kingdom compared to the major human and elven nations, but the vampires who lived there were notoriously powerful.","Their natural regenerative abilities were extraordinary, and consuming blood allowed them to recover from injuries at an astonishing rate.","Even among supernatural races, vampires were feared for their physical resilience.","But their relationship with humanity and the elves had always been hostile.","Vampires particularly favored the blood of humans and elves, with the blood of high elves being considered especially valuable.","That hostility eventually led to a devastating war.","Humanity and the Elven Kingdom eventually joined forces against Vespermark.","The vampire kingdom was simply too small to withstand two major powers attacking it simultaneously.","Noah continued reading historical records about the conflict.","The war had ended with the complete destruction of Vespermark. The vampires had been hunted down and exterminated. Be it women, children or old people.","According to the historical records, neither side had shown mercy.","Noah’s fingers slowly tightened around his phone.","’They really wiped out the entire race...’","He imagined what that must have looked like.","An entire kingdom surrounded by two powerful nations. There was no realistic way for a small island kingdom to survive such an attack.","It wasn’t really a war anymore. It had become a complete defeat followed by the destruction of an entire people.","A shiver ran down Noah’s spine.","\"That’s... brutal.\"","’There has to be more to this history.’","Noah leaned back against the headboard.","’If vampires really went extinct nearly a hundred years ago, then how could Bloodmoon Rot still be appearing? Maybe Marina’s sister wasn’t suffering from Bloodmoon Rot at all or maybe some vampires from House Bloodwyn had survived.’","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","’If even one highborn vampire survived the destruction of Vespermark, then this changes everything.’","He immediately shook his head.","\"Don’t jump to conclusions.\"","He reminded himself.","’I don’t even know if Marina’s sister has Bloodmoon Rot.’","For all he knew, her illness could be completely unrelated.","Still, the coincidence was too strange to ignore.","Ken had gone through great trouble to obtain an Everbloom Draught.","Marina had said the potion could allow her sister to run around again.","Noah stared at the ceiling.","\"There’s definitely something going on. Let’s see where this potion could be found.\"","He went back to tab of potion’s information. \"The fuck!!\" He couldn’t help but curse after reading more information.","It was written that to make Everbloom Draught potion it needs blood of a highborn vampire who posses that ability to spread disease. It is essential ingredient.","Because of this in current time if there exist this potions in world, then they were extremely rare, biggest chance to found them were within dungeons made by vampires."]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Browsing Information [2]","paragraphs":["He paused. \"I guess I need to study history more seriously too.\"","His curiosity had only grown. He wanted to know more about Vespermark.","More about the vampires.","Noah eventually sat up.","\"Enough thinking. Huge possibility that Ken might be like me... but with knowledge...\"","He placed his phone aside and got out of bed.","Nancy, who had been sleeping comfortably throughout his entire investigation, opened one golden eye because of the sound.","She watched Noah hurriedly walk toward his desk.","\"Meow...\"","Noah glanced back at her.","\"What?\"","Nancy stared at him for a few seconds.","Then she yawned lazily.","\"...\"","She simply closed her eyes again and went back to sleep.","Noah sighed.","\"Right. Of course. Why would you care?\"","He walked over to his desk. After sitting down, Noah reached into his storage ring and took out a thick notebook along with a pen.","This wasn’t an ordinary notebook. It was something Noah had started using specifically for dangerous information.","Whenever something suspicious happened to him, whenever he encountered an incident he couldn’t explain, or whenever he discovered something that might become important later, he wrote it down.","He had learned the hard way that relying entirely on memory was dangerous.","Especially in this world. Noah opened the notebook to a fresh page. He stared at the blank page for a moment.","Then he began writing. The first thing he recorded was the labyrinth.","He carefully documented everything he could remember from the moment he and Damien entered it.","From routes to monsters to the portal. Also the phenomenon happened after Noah vanished in portal.","How those creatures came out from the last boss’s body.","He wrote down every detail he could remember, even things that seemed insignificant.","He deliberately avoided writing anything in a vague manner. If he remembered something clearly, he wrote it down as fact.","After several pages, he reached the events involving Akari.","He carefully recorded how he had encountered her inside the mysterious realm and how they had eventually fought together to survive. he didn’t wrote anything about her bloodline.","He didn’t write down every single detail exactly as it had happened, but he made sure he had enough information to reconstruct the events later.","Eventually, he reached today’s events.","Noah turned to a new section.","Ken Takeane — Suspicious Activity","He began writing.","Ken Takeane was observed secretly meeting Marina behind the dormitory building.","After he was done he rubbed his forehead.","\"Why does everything around me have to be so complicated?\"","He sighed. Then his gaze drifted toward Nancy.","The black cat was still sleeping peacefully on his bed, completely unconcerned with the mysteries threatening to pile up around them.","Noah couldn’t help but smile. \"At least someone here has a peaceful life that I always wish.\"","Nancy’s ears twitched. But she didn’t open her eyes.","Noah kept staring at her then chuckled quietly. Then his expression became serious again.","He looked down at his notebook. \"I need to find out what Ken is planning.\"","He picked up his pen once more. \"And I need to find out whether Marina’s sister actually has Bloodmoon Rot.\"","If she did then the question wouldn’t simply be how she had contracted the disease.","The bigger question would be much more frightening. Were there still vampires alive in this world? If yes then definitely they have some dangerous role in future of this game, in future of this world.","Noah slowly closed the notebook.","Whatever the answer was, he had a feeling that this matter would eventually lead him somewhere he hadn’t expected.","----","\"Yes, Noah? Why did you call me?\"","\"Can’t I call you without a reason now?\" Noah asked, sounding genuinely hurt. \"Sigh... If you really want a reason, then it’s because I missed you.\"","He lay comfortably on his bed with Nancy resting on his chest. One hand gently stroked the little cat’s head, occasionally messing with her fur just to annoy her, while his other hand held the phone to his ear.","He was talking to one of the people dearest to him.","A soft chuckle came from the other end of the call.","\"Haha, don’t be so dramatic. And yes, you can call me even if you don’t have a reason. Just try not to do it when I’m busy.\"","It was Akari’s calm, familiar voice.","\"Hmm... I miss you.\"","\"Yes. Me too. So, did you go to the academy?\"","\"Yeah. Just today.\"","They continued talking for a while, jumping between random topics and casually sharing what had happened since they last spoke. Neither of them seemed particularly interested in ending the call.","After a while, however, Noah remembered the reason he’d wanted to speak with her.","\"Akari, I wanted to ask you something.\"","\"Sure. What is it?\"","\"Hmm...\" Noah hesitated for a moment before asking, \"Do you think vampires are still alive?\"","There was silence on the other end.","Akari didn’t say anything for a while. \"According to the records of our history...\" she finally began, her voice thoughtful, \"they’re supposed to be dead.\"","She continued \"But honestly, I wouldn’t completely believe those records. Vampires weren’t some unintelligent race of beasts or monsters that could simply disappear or get extinct from the world. They were an intelligent race, just like humans and elves.\"","Akari paused briefly.","\"Making an entire intelligent race completely disappear is almost impossible. So, I believe there are definitely some vampires still out there somewhere.\"","\"Hmm... okay.\"","\"But why the sudden interest in vampires?\"","\"Nothing serious. I was studying history and suddenly became curious about them. The war was really cruel.\"","\"Well, that’s how war is,\" Akari replied calmly. \"It happens between races, and sometimes even between humans themselves.\"","She paused before adding,","\"Don’t forget that my family and the Raigamine Duchy was once a separate kingdom. It was only after we lost a war against the Aurelian Empire that our kingdom became part of the empire.\"","\"Oh, right...\"","Noah fell silent for a moment, thinking about her words.","’So Akari also believes that the vampires might still be alive...’","His curiosity only deepened.","---","[A/N: Damn guys!! I actually forgot to upload Chapters yesterday!! I thought i uploaded but i didn’t!! Damn my goldfish memory!! Sorry!!]"]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: Away from Academy","paragraphs":["=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 724 [+112]","Speed: 737 [+120]","Stamina: 720 [+101]","Endurance: 712 [+104]","Charm: 803 [+103]","Mana: 7313 [+1100]","Core Rank: Condensed (High)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.3]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist], [Ice Blizzard], [Crystal Bloom], [Winter Howl]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Abilities: [Adaptive Learning], [Heart of Absolute Frost]","Active Ability: [Monarch’s Decree], [Puppet of the Frost Dragon]","Bloodline: [Monarch of the Frost]","===================","\"Damn, my powers have increased by quite a lot.\"","Noah looked over his status with satisfaction.","He had made tremendous progress in just six months since arriving in this world.","Well... technically, it had been much longer than six months.","He had spent seven months inside that mysterious realm, after all. But from the perspective of the outside world, only a month had passed.","And now, there was something else he wanted to try.","His newly acquired ability.","[Puppet of the Frost Dragon].","’How exactly does this Frost Dragon puppet work?’","He was eager to find out.","It was another morning, and today marked Noah’s first class of the second semester at Novaris Academy.","He glanced at the calendar.","Today was the 24th day of the sixth month, Year 2048.","After getting ready, Noah put on his academy uniform, a gray coat over a white shirt, accompanied by a red tie.","\"Finally, I have to attend lectures again...\"","He sighed and glanced toward the bed.","\"But damn, I’m already bored.\"","His gaze landed on Nancy, who was peacefully sleeping on the bed.","Noah stared at the cat for a few seconds.","\"You sleep all day. You’re so lucky. How good must your life be?\"","He couldn’t help but envy her carefree existence.","Unfortunately, unlike Nancy, he had responsibilities.","There was no point in complaining.","\"Sigh... let’s go. At least the instructor is Morgana. I can handle it.\"","With that, Noah left his dormitory room.","---","\"Is there something on my face?\"","Noah looked toward his left with a slightly confused expression.","Lyria was sitting beside him.","\"No... I mean, you never sat beside me before during class.\"","\"Well, there was a reason—\"","\"Because the two of us sit at the front, he used to avoid sitting beside us. But for some reason, he isn’t doing that anymore.\"","Arisha, sitting on Lyria’s other side, casually interrupted.","She spoke as though it were the most ordinary thing in the world.","\"She’s not wrong.\"","Noah couldn’t help but agree. There was no reason for him to hide it anymore.","\"It’s good to sit in the front. From now on, this is our fixed seat.\"","From Noah’s other side, Damien spoke.","\"Tch. I was hoping Arisha would sit here, but I guess there’s nothing I can do about it now.\"","\"Haha, you really don’t hide what you want.\"","Damien chuckled before patting Noah on the shoulder.","Noah glanced behind him.","A few seats away sat Ophelia.","The moment she noticed Noah’s gaze, she met his eyes and simply gave him a small nod.","Noah returned his attention to the front.","’Now I need to learn as much as possible about these side characters, especially the heroines.’","His expression became slightly thoughtful.","’Who knows? Maybe they have sad stories like Marina’s. I need to look into it.’","Just then, the classroom door opened.","A woman entered the room.","It was Morgana.","Her sky-blue hair was tied into a perfectly neat bun, while her amethyst eyes swept coldly across the entire classroom.","\"It appears everyone is present.\"","She walked toward the instructor’s desk.","\"Welcome back, everyone. The last month has been rather hectic. Monsters suddenly began emerging from an unknown location across various parts of the empire, including Novaris City itself.\"","Morgana placed one hand on the desk.","\"Fortunately, the situation has now been resolved. The academy also had to delay its reopening because of the incident.\"","Her cold gaze swept across the students once more.","\"But now, it is time to refocus on your studies and training.\"","She paused briefly.","\"I hope all of you are ready.\"","\"YES!!!\"","The students answered in unison.","\"Good.\"","Morgana nodded.","\"Now, let’s begin our first lecture.\"","---","Somewhere Far Away from Novaris Academy","In the largest city of the Aurellian Empire, a metropolis far grander than even Novaris City, stood the very heart of the empire.","Aurex Prime.","The magnificent city stretched across the horizon, filled with towering skyscrapers and beautiful modern buildings.","At the heart of the city, overlooking everything from atop a massive hill, stood the imperial palace.","It was enormous.","Its architecture combined modern grandeur with the majesty of an ancient royal fortress.","Inside the vast throne room, massive pillars stood along both sides, supporting the towering ceiling.","At the far end of the chamber was a grand staircase leading toward a majestic black-and-gold throne.","And upon that throne sat a man whose very presence carried the aura of a conqueror.","His dirty-blond hair was neatly combed, while a well-groomed beard framed his masculine features.","One arm rested casually on the throne’s armrest, while his other elbow supported his cheek.","His silver eyes stared forward with an indifferent expression.","He was one of the strongest human across the continent, Viserys Augustus, the Emperor of the strongest Empire, The Aurellian Empire.","A man with white hair stood beside his throne, reporting something to him. He was Baeon, an higher ranking minister in council and trusted person to Emepror.","\"Hmm... so the daughter of Narukami has returned.\"","Viserys’s expression remained indifferent.","\"That’s unexpected. But it is certainly interesting information to receive after I returned to my palace.\"","\"Your Majesty,\" Baeon continued respectfully, \"the monster hordes that had been emerging from the unknown location also stopped appearing and mysteriously perished on the very same day Lady Akari Narukami returned.\"","Viserys’s silver eyes narrowed slightly.","\"And here I have been traveling from place to place, searching for a solution to the situation.\"","His voice remained calm. \"Many others tried as well... yet no one succeeded.\"","He paused for a moment. \"Did you arrange a meeting with her?\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty. I have already sent a message to the Narukami family.\" He bowed his head.","\"Lady Akari has agreed to come here tomorrow to meet with His Imperial Majesty.\"","Viserys leaned back slightly against his throne. A faint glimmer appeared in his indifferent silver eyes."]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: New Dispute","paragraphs":["A week had passed since the academy reopened.","It was now the second week of the semester.","And today, something happened at the academy once again.","The cafeteria was unusually noisy. Students had gathered around something in the middle of the hall, creating a large crowd while excited voices echoed throughout the room.","Noah had just entered the cafeteria with Lyria and Arisha when the commotion immediately caught their attention.","The atmosphere felt strangely familiar.","Noah experienced a sudden sense of déjà vu.","It was almost identical to the atmosphere back when Damien had gotten into a fight with Edward.","\"What’s going on?\" Lyria wondered, looking toward the crowd.","\"Someone must be fighting,\" Arisha replied casually, as though there could hardly be any other explanation.","\"It must be Damien. He probably got into another fight.\"","\"Why do you think it must be him?\" Lyria asked.","\"Who else could it be? Don’t you remember? He got into a fight before, too.\"","\"Yes, but that doesn’t mean—\"","Before Lyria could finish her sentence, a voice from nearby interrupted them.","\"It’s Damien Ashworth! He got into an argument with someone!\"","A student nearby whispered excitedly to his friend before both of them hurried toward the crowd.","The three of them remained where they were for a moment.","\"Sigh... It’s really him,\" Lyria said helplessly. \"We should have joined the crowd earlier.\"","\"It’s Noah’s fault for not being able to finish that potion in time during alchemy class. And as if that wasn’t enough, he stopped both of us from going there with him.\"","Noah completely ignored Arisha’s complaint.","\"Putting that aside, let’s go and see who he’s arguing with this time.\"","The trio made their way through the crowd.","And when they finally reached the center, Noah’s expression changed.","Damien was standing there.","Emma stood behind him.","But opposite them was the last person Noah had expected to see.","A young man with dirty-blond hair and striking silver eyes stood proudly before them. He was handsome, sharp-featured, and roughly the same height as Noah.","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly.","’Prince Justinian Augustus.’","The second prince of the Aurellian Empire.","He was a second-year student at Novaris Academy.","’How the hell did Damien manage to get on his bad side?’","Justinian stood with an elegant, proud posture, his cold eyes fixed on Damien.","\"Damien, you should learn how to speak properly first. Surely, you understand who I am?\"","Damien looked slightly tense.","\"Your Highness, I didn’t mean it that way. I didn’t think you would take offense at what I said.\"","Emma immediately stepped forward and bowed.","\"Please forgive Damien Ashworth, Your Highness.\"","She kept her head lowered.","\"I apologize on his behalf.\"","Damien clenched his fists.","He clearly didn’t like seeing Emma apologize for something that was not her fault.","\"Emma, don’t apologize. You didn’t do anything wrong. And we are not at fault.\"","\"Then you should take responsibility for it, Damien.\"","Justinian took a step forward.","Several people standing behind him, his fellow second-year students and followers, remained silently behind him.","His gaze shifted toward Emma. \"And you are from the Hayes family... A count-ranked family, correct?\"","\"Yes, Your Grace.\"","Emma remained bowed, her voice slightly trembling as fear crept into her heart.","Damien was about to say something when another voice suddenly entered the conversation.","\"Oh my~ If it isn’t our esteemed Prince Justinian Augustus.\"","Everyone in the cafeteria turned toward the newcomer. And it was none other than Noah.","With a polite smile on his face, Noah walked toward Justinian. \"Greetings, Brother Justinian. It has been quite some time since last we crossed paths. I trust you hasn’t forgotten this humble man?\"","Justinian studied Noah for a moment. Then, a faint smirk appeared on his face.","\"Of course I remember you. How could I possibly forget the exiled son of House Eldritch, whose notorious habits were once the talk of noble circles?\"","Damien and Emma looked at Noah in surprise.","Noah, however, showed no reaction to the remark. His smile remained perfectly intact.","He walked forward and positioned himself between Damien and Justinian. \"It is indeed an honor that Your Highness still remembers me.\"","Noah glanced toward Damien before returning his attention to Justinian. \"Yet, judging by the present circumstances, it would seem that my friend has committed some offense against your highness. Though I know not the nature of his transgression, I humbly ask that Your Highness overlook his mistake.\"","Justinian let out a quiet chuckle. \"Oh, Noah. When did I ever say that I intended to punish him?\"","He tilted his head slightly. \"Why do you assume such a thing? Am I truly so fearsome in your eyes?\"","Noah maintained his polite smile. But internally, he was cursing. ’Of course you bastard. I know exactly what kind of piece of shit you are.’","As the son of a duke, Noah had naturally known the second prince since childhood. Justinian possessed everything expected of an imperial prince.","He was handsome, charming, elegant, and dignified. But Noah knew that those qualities were merely a mask.","Behind that refined appearance was a petty, arrogant, and selfish man who looked down upon commoners and rarely tolerated anything that displeased him.","Noah still didn’t know what Damien had said that had offended him.","Justinian’s expression showed no obvious anger. He was even smiling.","Yet Noah knew better. Something was wrong.","’Dammit. We never even crossed paths during the first semester. So why now?’","During the first semester, most of the conflicts had involved first-year students. But now that the second semester had begun,","Noah realized that students from the upper years might become involved as well. And if Justinian was now taking an interest in Damien.","’This is going to bring even more trouble into his life.’","\"Of course not, Your Highness.\" Noah’s smile never faltered.","\"Everyone knows that you to be a most benevolent and generous prince.\"","Justinian’s eyes narrowed slightly at the flattery, though his smile remained.","Noah then turned toward Damien. \"Damien, you should bow and offer them apology. Do not allow others to become entangled in your mistake, nor let another speak on your behalf. If you has earn, then face it by yourself.\"","Damien clenched his fist again. He clearly wasn’t pleased by Noah’s words.","But he glanced around. The crowd had grown considerably larger, and even Emma had bowed before the prince to apologize on his behalf.","Noah’s words were reasonable. After a brief hesitation, Damien finally relented.","He stepped forward and bowed to Justinian. \"I apologize for my mistake. I shouldn’t have said those words.\"","Justinian stared at Damien for a moment.","Then his expression softened into a faint smile.","\"See? It was not so difficult, was it?\" He spoke with the calm confidence of a senior instructing a junior.","\"As thy senior, I merely wished to teach the importance of accepting responsibility for one’s mistakes.\"","His gaze lingered on Damien. \"And you has done well. After all, you are the first-ranked student among the first years, Damien Ashworth.\"","He then looked around the cafeteria. \"And why have all of are gathered here?\"","His tone became slightly amused. \"This is a cafeteria, is it not? You all to be enjoying the meal rather than standing about and watching a trivial dispute.\"","The students immediately began dispersing.","One by one, the crowd returned to their tables, and within moments, the commotion that had filled the cafeteria began to fade.","Just as the situation seemed to be over, however, Justinian’s gaze wandered across the room.","His silver eyes suddenly stopped. They landed on Lyria. For a brief moment, his eyes widened ever so slightly.","Then, slowly his smile grew a little wider."]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: We are close...","paragraphs":["\"Oh my, if it isn’t Lady Lyria Sunweave.\" Justinian’s expression brightened as he approached, a charming smile spreading across his face.","Lyria, who was standing beside Arisha, immediately straightened and gave him a light bow. \"Greetings, Your Highness.\"","Arisha followed her lead and bowed as well. \"Greetings, Your Highness.\"","\"There is no need for such formalities. We are within the academy, after all. You may simply address me as Senior.\"","His tone was polite and friendly. And this time it looked genuine, unlike how it felt false mask while talking with Noah and Damien.","Both girls straightened at his words.","\"It’s been a while, Senior,\" Lyria said respectfully. \"And please don’t call me ’Lady’ while we’re here. I’m merely a student and your junior.\"","At her words, Justinian’s smile widened slightly. \"Very well, Junior Lyria.\"","His silver eyes then shifted toward Arisha, taking in her equally striking appearance. \"And you?\"","\"Arisha Willow.\"","\"Oh. Junior Arisha.\"","Noah watched the exchange from the side, his eyebrow twitching slightly.","’Is this bastard interested in Lyria or something?I didn’t like it.’","His eyes narrowed thoughtfully.","’Let’s test it.’ Without giving anyone time to react, Noah stepped forward and moved beside Lyria.","\"It appears you know Lyria quite well, Senior.\"","Before anyone could question what he was doing, Noah casually placed an arm around Lyria’s shoulders and gently pulled her toward him.","Her soft side of big chest pressed against his side. Lyria let out a small gasp. \"No-Noah?!\"","She looked at him in surprise, her pink eyes widening as a warm blush quickly spread across her cheeks.","\"What are you doing?\"","Noah calmly met her gaze. His fingers gave her shoulder a gentle squeeze, almost as if reassuring her.","His expression remained perfectly calm. His eyes seemed to tell her without words.","As if he was trying to say, ’Just go along with it.’","Lyria stared at him for a moment, confused and flustered.","Arisha, meanwhile, raised a single eyebrow. Damien and Emma looked equally stunned watching from side, they were also just few steps away.","Even several students who had been about to leave stopped in their tracks and turned around to watch.","But among all of them, one reaction immediately caught Noah’s attention.","Justinian’s expression had turned icy cold. \"What is the meaning of this, Noah?\"","His previously charming smile had vanished. \"Touching Junior Lyria in such a manner is most inappropriate. You cannot simply—\"","\"Your Highness—\" Noah paused. \"Ah, I mean, Senior.\"","He smiled politely. \"I’m quite close with Lyria, and she doesn’t mind it.\"","Noah looked down at Lyria. \"Right, Lyria? Or are you angry?\"","\"I-I mean...\" Lyria’s face became even redder. \"I’m mean I’m certainly not angry... but we’re in public, so this is...\"","\"Come on, why worry about what others think?\" Noah smiled casually. \"We’re close, aren’t we? I don’t think we need to hide it.\"","Justinian’s jaw tightened. His teeth clenched slightly, though he quickly concealed his reaction. His gaze shifted toward Lyria.","Her face was flushed with embarrassment, her expression shy and flustered. Clearly, he wasn’t enjoying what he was seeing.","And Noah noticed. ’This guy really does have something for Lyria. Dammit! My innocent saint is in danger!’","Noah’s expression remained perfectly composed despite the alarm bells going off inside his head.","Justinian took a slow breath, seemingly forcing himself to calm down.","He then looked back at Noah. \"I was not aware... that the two of you were like this.\"","His smile returned, though it looked somewhat forced. \"Well, regardless, I shall take my leave. It was a pleasure meeting you all.\"","With that, Justinian turned around and began walking away.","Noah’s eyes widened. ’Wait!’","\"Senior—\"","\"Noah!\" Before he could call after him, Damien suddenly rushed over.","Emma followed closely behind. \"What the hell was that?! When did this happen?\"","Noah glanced at Damien and clicked his tongue internally. ’Not right now.’","By the time he looked back, Justinian was already walking away with his followers, leaving them behind.","’Well...’","Noah sighed. ’It’s not like that me clearing things will change anything.’","Still, he couldn’t deny one thing. ’But damn that expression on his face was pretty amusing. I liked it.’","\"Noah, I’m asking you something!\"","Damien’s voice brought him back to reality.","Noah looked at him and sighed. \"Whatever you’re thinking, it’s not like that between me and Lyria.\"","\"Then why did you act like that?\" Emma asked in confusion. Damien nodded, clearly having the same question.","\"And could you release the poor girl from your clutches?\" Arisha pointed toward Lyria.","Only then did Noah realize something. He was still holding Lyria against him. He immediately released her and stepped away.","\"Ahem. Sorry about that Lyria.\"","He coughed lightly, pretending nothing unusual had happened. \"I only did that because I wanted to understand something.\"","\"Understand what?\" Lyria asked, still looking slightly flustered.","She didn’t seem angry, though. \"I didn’t push you away because I knew you must have had a reason for doing that.\"","Noah nodded. \"I did.\"","He glanced toward where Justinian had disappeared. \"I’ll explain everything while we eat lunch.\"","Just then, a loud voice echoed across the cafeteria.","\"Hello, everyone! What’s up? Why are you guys just standing around here? Did something happen?\"","Leonard and Kaelan had just entered the cafeteria and were making their way toward the group. Leonard looked around at everyone’s expressions.","Noah glanced at them. \"Well...\"","A faint smile appeared on his face. \"You two certainly missed something amazing.\" he shook his head.","Then he looked at Damien. \"Also, Damien, I would like to understand what you did to make the prince angry.\"","Damien frowned but nodded. \"I didn’t do anything wrong. That man just got offended over something so small. Let’s find a table. I’ll tell you all about it.\"","And so, the group once again carried their lunches over to a table and sat down.","Whatever Damien was about to tell them, this conversation might turn out to be either very interesting or maybe dangerous."]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: About Prince Justinian","paragraphs":["\"So, you mean...\" Noah paused, recounting everything Damien had told him. \"Let me get this straight. You were simply walking when he bumped into your shoulder. Then you told him, ’Watch where you’re going, bro, or you might get hurt.’\"","\"Yes,\" Damien replied, sitting across from Noah. \"But I said it in a friendly tone. I was even smiling.\"","\"Huh...\" Noah nodded slowly. \"And the prince didn’t like your friendly tone, so he told you that wasn’t how you should speak to him and warned you to watch your tone.\"","\"Exactly.\"","\"And then you said, ’What’s wrong with my tone, brother? I only told you to be more careful next time. If you were offended, then I’m sorry. But there’s no need to get angry over something so small.’\"","\"Yup.\"","\"And that made him even angrier.\" Noah sighed and shook his head.","\"What a shitty way to get on the bad side of a prince. Well, if you were a beautiful girl, you might have been forgiven more easily.\"","Damien’s lips twitched. \"Tch. I didn’t even know he was a prince at first. It took me a while to recognize him. If I’d known from the beginning, I would’ve apologized right away.\"","\"No, you wouldn’t have.\"","Noah gave him a knowing look. \"I know you. You would’ve tried to escalate the situation even further because you thought you weren’t in the wrong.\"","Damien immediately fell silent.","Because Noah was right.","\"Well, thanks to Noah, we were able to calm the situation down,\" Emma said from Damien’s left.","Noah looked at her in mild surprise.","She had actually said something good about him.","\"True. Thanks, Noah,\" Damien added.","\"It’s fine.\"","\"Shit! I missed the drama!\" Leonard’s stunned voice suddenly came from beside them.","The group had chosen a table in one of the quieter corners of the cafeteria, away from the main crowd. With all of them sitting close together, the surrounding noise made it difficult for anyone nearby to hear their conversation.","Leonard had taken the seat beside Arisha, while Arisha sat to Noah’s right.","\"It was a pretty serious situation, to be honest,\" Leonard continued. \"If Damien had ended up on the bad side of Prince Justinian...\"","\"Why?\" Arisha asked.","\"Well, since you’re not from a noble family, you might not know this.\"","Leonard lowered his voice. \"Prince Justinian is a two-faced man. He acts kind and polite toward everyone, but he’s extremely petty, arrogant, prideful, and... well, let’s just say he’s not someone you want as an enemy.\"","He glanced around before continuing. \"Most nobles around our age, as well as those in his generation, know what he’s really like. We just pretend we don’t.\"","\"Are you sure?\" Arisha asked again, her expression skeptical.","\"Yes.\"","Before Leonard could elaborate, Lyria spoke.","\"He’s right. I remember something from a few years ago.\"","Everyone turned toward her.","\"During a banquet held by the imperial family for the First Prince’s birthday, a young man from a count’s family made a joke while speaking with Justinian.\"","Lyria’s expression became thoughtful.","\"He said something about hoping Justinian would become more like his older brother, the First Prince. I was there that night, so I remember it clearly.\"","She glanced around the table. \"Kaelan, Noah, and even Leonard were there as well.\"","\"And what happened afterward?\" Damien asked curiously.","\"Justinian simply laughed it off at the time,\" Kaelan answered.","\"But a few weeks later, we heard that the same young man had been accused of stealing a brooch belonging to Prince Justinian—a brooch that had been given to him by his mother.\"","Leonard snorted. \"It was obviously fabricated. We all knew it.\"","\"Damn...\" Damien’s expression changed. \"Isn’t that going too far?\"","\"What happened to the guy?\" Arisha asked.","\"Nothing serious, apparently,\" Noah answered.","He leaned back slightly.","\"According to what I heard, he eventually begged Justinian for forgiveness and even knelt before him. Justinian supposedly forgave him afterward, and that young man eventually became one of his followers.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"And he was standing behind Justinian earlier.\"","Damien swallowed. \"That’s dangerous.\"","He paused. \"I really am lucky.\"","\"True,\" Arisha muttered.","Leonard shrugged. \"Though you probably would’ve only had to deal with some bullying from his followers.\"","He paused. \"Or something worse. I honestly have no idea.\"","Damien’s expression stiffened. \"Please don’t say things like that so casually.\"","Everyone ignored him.","Arisha turned her attention toward Noah. \"Now tell us why you did that to Lyria.\"","Noah shrugged. \"I just had a feeling...\" He glanced around the table before lowering his voice. \"I thought Justinian might be interested in Lyria.\"","Everyone became slightly more attentive.","\"So I wanted to confirm it.\" Noah continued.","\"I acted as though Lyria and I were extremely close. And when I did that, his expression immediately changed. He was clearly annoyed and angry.\"","He tapped his fingers lightly against the table. \"That pretty much confirmed my suspicion that he might actually have feelings for her.\"","Silence fell around the table.","Even Lyria blinked in surprise.","\"Then... it might really be true.\"","Noah looked at her. \"You had doubts too? Has he approached you before?\"","\"Yes...\"","Lyria nodded. \"He spoke to me a few times during the first semester, but it was mostly just polite greetings.\"","She sighed softly. \"I never thought much of it.\"","Emma frowned. \"Noah... doesn’t that put you on the bad side of the prince?\"","Noah pressed his lips into a thin line. \"Yeah...\"","He rubbed the back of his neck. \"I mean, the way I was holding Lyria and the way she was blushing probably made us look like a couple.\"","He glanced at Lyria. \"It looked like I was openly accepting the relationship while she was just too shy to admit it.\"","Lyria’s cheeks immediately turned bright red.","Noah noticed her reaction and awkwardly looked away.","Arisha also waited for his answer.","After a moment, Noah simply shrugged.","\"Whatever. I can clear up the misunderstanding whenever I want. It’s not a big problem.\"","\"Hmm...\" Kaelan folded his arms. \"But a lot of students saw you. There are bound to be rumors about the two of you.\"","\"Re-really?\" Lyria’s pink eyes widened. \"Rumors?\"","Noah casually waved his hand. \"Who cares? They’re just rumors.\"","\"Then when are you going to clear things up with the prince?\" Arisha asked, resting her chin against her hand.","\"Not for now.\"","A small smirk appeared on Noah’s face.","\"W-what? Why not?\" Lyria asked, visibly flustered.","\"Well, let him believe it for now.\"","Noah leaned back in his chair. \"Maybe he’ll lose interest in you and give up.\"","Leonard shook his head. \"He doesn’t look like the type of person who gives up easily.\"","\"If that happens, I’ll clear things up.\" Noah paused. \"Or maybe I won’t.\"","He smiled mischievously. \"Either way, we should protect my—\" He stopped himself. \"I mean... our cute Lyria.\"","Lyria’s entire face flushed with warmth.","\"U-Ugh...\"","She lowered her head, unable to look at anyone.","Arisha simply shook her head. \"Sure. We should.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement before returning to their lunch.","Their conversation gradually shifted to other topics as they continued eating.","None of them noticed that, from another corner of the cafeteria, someone had been quietly watching their table the entire time."]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Puppet of the Frost Dragon","paragraphs":["Noah stood alone in one corner of the training ground.","The reason was simple. He wanted to test his newly acquired ability.","[Puppet of the Frost Dragon]","Considering everything he had gone through, the rewards he had received had honestly felt rather underwhelming.","At least, they had seemed that way to his current self. But there was only one way to know whether the ability was truly disappointing.","Test it and judge it.","Noah cracked his fingers one after another, then stretched his arms and rolled his shoulders.","\"Alright. Let’s see what you’ve got.\"","He raised one hand and slowly began channeling his mana. The moment he activated the ability, the atmosphere around him changed.","The temperature dropped sharply.","A thin layer of frost immediately spread across the ground beneath his feet, while countless fragments of ice began materializing out of thin air. They were beautiful, almost like translucent crystals carved from pure winter, shimmering faintly beneath the morning light.","More and more ice gathered around Noah.","The fragments began circling his body, slowly at first, before picking up speed. His mana started draining rapidly.","’So it consumes quite a lot of mana just to activate...’","The swirling ice suddenly intensified.","A miniature blizzard erupted around Noah, its freezing winds whipping against his clothes and sending countless snowflakes and ice particles spiraling through the air.","Whoosh!","The blizzard shot forward.","It continued expanding as it moved, growing larger and larger while the surrounding wind accelerated. The swirling mass of frost soon became several times larger than Noah himself.","And then, within the center of the raging blizzard.","Something began to form.","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","’It’s forming.’","At first, four enormous claws made of ice emerged from within the storm.","The claws slowly transformed into powerful legs. From there, the structure continued growing.","A massive body took shape, followed by a long, thick tail that stretched behind it. Then came the neck, rising higher and higher, until finally a dragon’s head emerged.","Two sharp horns formed above its skull. One after another, layers of crystalline scales spread across its entire body, each one looking as though it had been carved from the purest ice.","The blizzard gradually weakened.","The violent winds slowed. Snow and frost drifted harmlessly through the air before settling onto the ground.","And finally, the creature was revealed, it was a dragon.","It was nowhere near the size of Akari’s true dragon form, of course. Compared to that monstrous scale, this creature was practically tiny.","But that did not mean it was small. From the tip of its snout to the end of its tail, the Frost Dragon was approximately ten meters long.","Its massive wings unfolded from its back.","Each wing stretched roughly ten meters from one end to the other, their surfaces composed entirely of beautiful translucent ice.","It was more than large enough for Noah to sit comfortably on its back and fly.","Noah stared at the creature in fascination. Then he noticed something strange.","’Wait...’","The dragon was moving. Not because Noah had commanded it.","It was moving on its own. Noah could somehow feel a connection between them, a strange, almost instinctive bond.","He could sense its presence as clearly as he could sense his own mana. A smile slowly appeared on his face.","He didn’t say anything. Instead, he simply looked at the Frost Dragon.","’Look at me.’","The moment the thought entered his mind.","The dragon turned its enormous head. Its glacier-like eyes focused directly on Noah. They were cold and emotionless, almost devoid of any natural emotion. Yet there was no hostility in them.","There was only obedience.","Noah’s smile widened. \"So you really can understand me...\"","He walked toward the dragon. As he approached, the Frost Dragon lowered its massive head toward him, almost as though it were willingly offering itself.","Noah reached out and placed his hand against its head. The surface was freezing cold.","Yet the cold did not hurt him. Instead, the ice seemed to welcome his touch.","Noah gently patted its head. \"Hah...\"","He glanced at his remaining mana and sighed. \"That took roughly one-fourth of my mana just to create you.\"","He looked back at the Frost Dragon.","\"And your strength...\"","Noah narrowed his eyes slightly as he sensed its power.","\"It should be around the same level as my current core rank.\"","A huge grin spread across his face.","’This is actually amazing. When I wiill reach mythical rank then I can create a mythical rank frost dragon!!’","For someone who had expected the ability to be disappointing, Noah was now thoroughly impressed.","Unfortunately his excitement didn’t last very long.","\"A dragon?!\"","\"That’s a real dragon!\"","Noah froze. He slowly turned toward the source of the voices.","A few meters away, several students had been training. Some had stopped what they were doing and were now staring at the Frost Dragon with expressions of complete shock.","Others had gathered around them, pointing at the enormous creature.","Noah blinked.","’Hmm...’","He turned his attention back toward his newly created puppet.","An idea suddenly came to him. Noah raised his right arm, and decided to perform something that he always wanted to do.","\"Frosty!\"","The dragon’s glacier-colored eyes shifted toward him.","Noah pointed forward. \"Flame Thrower!\"","He did a command like how those trainers from Pokemoon anime used to do. But what came out of his mouth was most common attack in that anime by Charlizaard, forgetting his puppet is ice user.","So there was absolute silence after her spoke that.","Noah remained frozen in place. The students stared at him as if he had suddenly lost his mind.","The Frost Dragon tilted its head slightly. It looked at Noah. Then it looked at the students. Then it opened its enormous jaws.","Noah’s expression changed.","\"Well, I mean—frost—\"","BOOOOM!","A brilliant blue-white stream of freezing flames erupted from the dragon’s mouth. It shot directly toward the students.","\"The hell?! RUN!\"","\"You madman!\"","\"NOAH!\"","The students scattered in every direction. The blue frost-fire crashed into the ground with a thunderous roar.","CRACK!","A layer of ice instantly spread across everything the flames touched. The ground froze solid.","Patches of frost rapidly expanded outward, covering the training area in a beautiful but terrifying layer of blue-white ice.","Fortunately, there had been no intention to actually harm anyone, and the students had managed to escape the attack.","Noah stared at the frozen ground. His eyes sparkled.","’This...’ His gaze slowly shifted toward the Frost Dragon. ’This thing is amazing!’","He couldn’t help but feel excited. Not only could it fight independently, but it could apparently interpret his commands as well.","Although perhaps he should work on his naming skills.","Noah’s expression became thoughtful.","’ So the dragon was created using one-fourth of my mana...’","He rubbed his chin.","’That means it has roughly that much mana stored within its body.’","His eyes narrowed as he continued analyzing the ability.","’And if it runs out of mana, I’ll have to supply it with more mana to maintain its physical form and also to use magic.’","That explained the connection he could feel between them.","The Frost Dragon wasn’t simply a summoned creature. It was a puppet created from Noah’s own mana.","As long as he continued supplying it with mana, the Frost Dragon could remain active.","The dragon slowly lowered its head before standing proudly, its massive wings folding against its body.","Noah walked over and gave one of its enormous legs a satisfied pat.","\"Good job.\"","The Frost Dragon remained perfectly still.","Noah nodded approvingly. ’I really wish I had a cool frost-fire attack like that too.’","He looked at the frozen training ground. Then at the Frost Dragon. Then back at the frozen ground.","\"...Maybe I should learn one if possible... but how?\""]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: First Prince Justinian, and now...","paragraphs":["The days passed faster than Noah expected.","He kept wondering when the next incident would occur, yet for some reason, everything had been far too peaceful.","Nearly three weeks had passed since the academy reopened, and so far, Noah had done little more than train and practice.","And that, ironically, was beginning to make him nervous.","Noah sat on a bench at the edge of the training ground, resting his back against it as he stared at the evening sky.","He let out a long sigh.","He wanted to explore another dungeon and experience something exciting, but after what he had gone through inside the labyrinth with Damien, a part of him also wanted to stay as far away from dungeons as possible.","’There has to be something troublesome going on.’","His instincts refused to believe that things could remain this peaceful for long.","’Even Prince Justinian hasn’t done anything against Damien or me.’","Noah narrowed his eyes slightly.","’Though I’ve seen him a few times since then. He didn’t say anything, but the hostility in his eyes was obvious.’","Fortunately, nothing had happened yet. After sitting there for a while longer, Noah finally decided to return to his dormitory.","It was already evening. He stood up from the bench and made his way through the academy’s corridors.","Even at this hour, the halls remained lively.","Students walked around in groups, chatting with their friends after finishing their daily training and classes. Some were discussing their lessons, while others were simply enjoying their free time.","Then Noah noticed something else.","A few pairs of students men and women were walking together while holding hands.","Their faces were slightly flushed, and their expressions were filled with the unmistakable embarrassment of young couples enjoying their time together.","Noah clicked his tongue.","Tch.","’They’re enjoying romance while I’m over here worrying about what kind of disaster is going to fall on my head next.’","He couldn’t help but feel bitter about his life.","Even the one woman who had managed to make his heart genuinely beat faster had been separated from him before he could fall head overs for her.","Noah sighed. ’Maybe I already am...’","He paused. Then another thought suddenly entered his mind.","’Hmm... Since I’m living in a new world where having multiple wives isn’t exactly unusual... should I try it?’","His imagination began running wild.","’Become incredibly strong, make a fortune, marry several beautiful women, have lots of children, and then watch them grow up and fight over my property and legacy—’","Noah’s expression stiffened. ’...What the hell am I thinking?’","That train of thought had gone in a very strange direction. He definitely shouldn’t be fantasizing about enjoying the sight of his own children fighting over his wealth.","Though the idea of having multiple wives and a large family wasn’t exactly unpleasant.","Noah rubbed his chin.","’Maybe I should create my own clan someday, after I survive all the dangers surrounding me.’","A faint smile appeared on his face.","’ Well, only if there’s no way for me to return to my original world . ’","The thought immediately made that smile disappear. A bitter feeling settled in his chest as he look down at floor.","He had once been determined to find a way back home. But after spending so much time living as Noah Eldritch, things had gradually changed.","He had grown accustomed to this world, to his new identity, to his family, friends, to the people he had met.","Even his memories of his former life no longer felt as vivid as they once had.","’I can’t let that happen.’ He clenched his fist slightly. ’I can’t let myself forget my original life completely.’","Thud!","Something suddenly bumped into his shoulder.","Noah’s thoughts were interrupted. \"I’m sorry! I wasn’t looking where I was going.\"","He instinctively raised a hand to apologize as well. But the moment he looked at the person in front of him and he froze.","A bead of sweat slowly rolled down his forehead. He couldn’t tell whether it was because of the hours of training he had endured earlier.","Or because of the person standing before him.","’Why?’","His expression twitched. ’First Prince Justinian, and now...’","Standing before him was a beautiful woman with long, maroon-colored hair cascading down her back.","Her silver eyes were cold and sharp.","She looked at Noah with an indifferent expression, as though he were nothing more than an insignificant passerby.","\"Noah Eldritch.\"","Her voice was calm. \"You should look where you are going. Walking while staring at the ground is a rather bad habit.\"","Noah’s mouth twitched. He immediately recognized her.","\"Your Highness—\"","\"No need to address me like that.\"","She interrupted him without hesitation.","Noah quickly adjusted his attitude. \"Huh... Senior Viserra, then. It is a pleasure to meet you, and I apologize for my mistake.\"","’Shit.’","His expression remained polite, but his thoughts were anything but.","’Another dangerous person. First Prince Justinian, and now her? Why am I meeting all these troublesome people during this semester?’","Noah had only seen her once during his first semester, and even then, it had been from a distance. But he knew exactly who she was.","Viserra Augustus.","The First Princess of the Aurellian Empire. A third-year student at Novaris Academy.","If Justinian was a two-faced man who presented himself as kind and courteous while hiding his arrogant and petty nature beneath that mask, Viserra was different.","She didn’t rely on the same sort of facade.","According to what Noah’s elder brother had told him two years ago, Viserra was far more cunning and manipulative.","She was the kind of woman who would use people however she pleased if doing so brought her closer to whatever goal she had set for herself.","And despite being only twenty-two years old, she possessed an exceptionally sharp mind.","Noah had never interacted with her personally before. So he had no idea why she had suddenly approached him now.","Viserra studied him silently for several seconds.","Her silver eyes narrowed slightly, as though she were examining something hidden beneath his appearance.","A faint, amused smile appeared on her lips.","\"Noah Eldritch...\" She tilted her head slightly. \"You have changed quite a bit since the last time I saw you.\"","Noah maintained his polite expression. \"People change. The time I spent after being exiled from my family taught me many things. Most of them, I had to learn on my own.\"","Viserra’s smile deepened slightly.","For a moment, she said nothing. Her gaze continued to linger on him, as though she were assessing him from head to toe.","Then she finally spoke. \"I suppose it was fortunate that I met you today.\"","\"Hmm?\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Pardon?\"","Viserra turned around. \"I wanted to speak with you.\"","She began walking down the corridor without waiting for a response. \"Follow me.\"","Noah remained standing there for a moment. He stared at her back.","’What does she want from me?’ His instincts were screaming that following her was probably a terrible idea.","Unfortunately, ignoring the First Princess of the Aurellian Empire probably wasn’t a particularly wise option either.","---","She led Noah to a secluded corridor of the academy.","Noah looked around and saw that no one else was there.","She stopped near an open window and leaned against it. The soft evening breeze made her hair sway gently.","As someone who had always appreciated beautiful women, Noah couldn’t deny that the princess was beautiful. However, he didn’t feel the same attraction toward her that he felt toward Arisha, Lyria, or Akira.","\"So, Noah.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"A few weeks ago... my brother Justinian had a heated moment with... one of your classmates named Damien, am I right?\"","\"Yes, that’s right...\"","\"Hmm. But it was resolved... You stepped in, and everything went well... but...\"","Her silver eyes stared directly at him.","\"Never would I have expected you to be in a relationship with Lyria of Sunweave. You do know what would happen if word reached her father... or perhaps it already has...\"","Noah’s lips twitched.","To be honest, all he knew about Lyria’s father was that he was a devoted follower of the Sun God and supposedly a kind-hearted man.","But perhaps that wasn’t the whole story.","’I guess this might become more problematic than I initially expected... but well not like I accepted or reveal with my mouth that we are actually in relationship. This is what people think...’","---","[A/N: Hello, guys! I know you must be cursing me and wondering, \"Why is this bastard author only uploading one Chapter again?\"","Well, I’m focusing more on the story right now, especially the big families and the important characters from them. For example, I’ve just introduced two new characters, so I want to take my time and develop things carefully instead of rushing through them.","Also, guys, the novel did pretty badly last month. We didn’t get many new readers, so please support the novel by sending some gifts. I know it’s shameless of me to ask, but maybe, just maybe, I’ll make one reader’s wish come true for the MC if they send a Super Gift.","Just pray that the request isn’t too weird or crazy!]"]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: You have my support","paragraphs":["Now standing beside Viserra, Noah quietly wondered what he should say next.","’Should I tell her there’s nothing between Lyria and me and clear up the misunderstanding?’","Before he could decide, Viserra broke the silence. \"To be honest, I have nothing to do with the matter. It is your life, after all. Though it’s very bad situation for a exiled son and a daughter of another duke to be in relationship.\"","She paused for a moment before continuing. \"And you should know that my brother seems to have some interest in Lyria Sunweave.\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","’Wait...Is she worried for her brother and want me to leave Lyria? When did she start caring about her brother’s love life?’","As far as he remembered, Viserra and Justinian were half-siblings born to different mothers. They were members of the same imperial family, but they had never appeared particularly close.","’Something feels strange about this.’","Rather than wait for her to explain further, Noah decided to speak first. \"So, Senior... are you asking me to stay away from Lyria?\"","Viserra raised an eyebrow. Then a soft chuckle escaped her lips. \"What? Why would I want that? I am not some evil woman.\"","A smile slowly bloomed across her face. \"Quite the opposite. I am telling you not to fear my brother.\"","Her silver eyes narrowed slightly with amusement. \"You have my support. Do not leave her.\"","Noah blinked.","’Yep. This is how it should be. She doesn’t like her brother. She definitely hate him.’","In fact, she seemed almost delighted by the fact that the woman Justinian had taken an interest in already had someone close to her, maybe have lover.","Noah deliberately widened his eyes. \"You... you really mean that?\"","\"Of course.\"","Viserra’s smile remained. \"Do you doubt the word of a member of the imperial family?\"","\"Of course not.\" Noah immediately bowed. \"I am deeply grateful that you are willing to support me.\"","But he was also confused . ’ Should I pretend that Lyria and I are already in a relationship? No...’","That would be too risky. There was no need to create another unnecessary complication, especially with someone as cunning as Viserra.","’I’ll tell her a half-truth instead. I don’t want to create unnecessary trouble with the princess either.’","Noah straightened his posture.","\"But, Senior...\"","\"Yes?\"","\"There has been a misunderstanding between Lyria and me... and, well, among the students.\"","Viserra frowned slightly. \"What misunderstanding?\"","\"The truth is...\" Noah hesitated. He lowered his gaze, as though struggling to find the right words. \"Lyria and I are not in a relationship.\"","Silence.","Viserra’s expression froze. She slowly uncrossed her arms. Then she looked directly at Noah. \"You two are not in a relationship?\"","\"Yes.\" He replied.","Her eyes narrowed. \"Then how could you act so intimately with her? You touched her and held her in front of everyone.\"","Her voice had become colder. The amusement and delight that had been present only moments ago disappeared almost instantly.","\"There was a reason.\"","\"Then explain.\" She ask for explanation.","Noah took a small breath. \"You see, I am very close to Lyria, but only as a friend. She trusts me, and because of that, she doesn’t mind normal physical contact between us.\"","He paused. \"But...\"","Noah’s expression became slightly embarrassed. \"I... I actually love her.\"","As he said those words, he deliberately avoided Viserra’s eyes. A faint flush appeared on his cheeks.","Viserra stared at him. The coldness in her silver eyes slowly disappeared. \"You love her...\"","\"Yes.\"","Noah nodded. \"That day, His Highness Prince Justinian was showing a great deal of interest in Lyria.\"","He lowered his head slightly. \"And, well...\"","His voice became quieter. \"I became jealous.\"","Viserra’s eyebrows rose.","\"So I intervened. That’s why I held her like that.\"","\"Oh...\"","Her expression softened. \"So that’s what happened.\"","\"Yes.\"","Noah gave an awkward smile.","\"I... I’ve been trying to express my feelings to Lyria through my actions. I think she has already noticed how I feel, but she hasn’t given me an answer yet. And that day she didn’t push me away.\"","He lowered his gaze again. \"It seems she is confused about her own feelings as well.\"","Viserra fell silent. She crossed her arms once again and began thinking deeply about what Noah had just told her.","Meanwhile, Noah maintained the expression of a young man desperately trying to win the heart of the woman he loved.","Inside, however, ’Good. Good. This should be enough. I was worried she might ask me to stay close with Lyria, don’t hide it or do something that could provoke Justinian even further. But with this explanation, there shouldn’t be any problem. At least... I hope so.’","After several seconds, Viserra finally spoke. \"Hmm...\"","A faint smile returned to her lips. \"Interesting.\"","She looked at Noah. \"Regardless, you have my support. Do not stop pursuing the girl you love simply because of Justinian. And you have changed a lot, also you are at second rank in first year. That’s amazing achievement.\"","Noah immediately nodded. \"Yes, Senior. I won’t. And thanks for compliment.\"","A polite smile appeared on his face. ’It worked.’","Noah inwardly breathed a sigh of relief. ’’I guess that’s all she wanted to talk about.’","He had expected the First Princess to summon him for something important or perhaps some serious political matter. And Noah was bad at politics, that’s for sure.","Instead, they had spent their time discussing his supposed relationship with Lyria.","’What a strange conversation.’","Noah was about to say something when Viserra suddenly spoke again.","\"By the way...\" She smiled. \"There is something else I wanted to ask you.\"","Noah paused.","\"Yes?\"","\"Tell me about Damien Ashworth.\"","Viserra’s smile remained as she looked directly at him. \"Your friend and classmate.\"","Noah’s expression remained calm, but his eyes narrowed slightly.","\"I already know about him. After all, he holds the first rank among the first-year students.\"","She paused briefly. \"But I want to know more about him from someone who is actually close to him.\"","Noah sighed inwardly. ’Well, well, well... Here it comes. The protagonist is attracting attention from another important character for absolutely no reason.’","He resisted the urge to sigh aloud. \"Of course.\"","Noah smiled politely. \"What would you like to know about him?\""]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: He definitely knows","paragraphs":["Another day.","Noah yawned as he walked toward his classroom, his hands casually tucked into his pockets. Just yesterday, he had ended up having a rather unexpected conversation with Viserra Augustus.","And what could he say about it? The conversation had started with Lyria and the misunderstanding surrounding their relationship.","Somehow, it had ended with Viserra asking him several questions about Damien. She hadn’t asked too many, but the questions themselves had been important.","For example, she had asked about the labyrinth incident, the very incident during which Noah had disappeared.","Of course, Noah hadn’t told her the whole truth.","From the way Viserra had reacted, Noah was fairly certain she hadn’t completely believed his explanation either.","She had also asked whether Damien was currently in a relationship, whether he liked anyone, what kind of personality he had, and even what sort of things he enjoyed.","At the time, Noah had simply answered carefully. But afterward, one question had remained stuck in his mind.","’Does she have a crush on Damien?’ Noah shook his head. ’No. That’s not possible.’","Viserra was the First Princess of the empire.","Damien was a commoner who had risen to become the top-ranked first-year student. There were certainly worse possibilities, but Noah couldn’t imagine that being the reason.","Besides, Viserra had explicitly told him that he could tell Damien about her questions if he wanted.","’Then there has to be another reason.’","Noah frowned slightly.","’ What could she possibly want with Damien?’","He hadn’t been able to figure it out.","\"NOAH!\"","A loud voice suddenly broke through his thoughts. Noah blinked and turned around.","Damien was approaching him with his usual enormous grin. The moment he caught up, Damien raised a hand.","\"Wassup, man?\"","\"Nothing much.\"","Noah glanced at him. \"You’re early today.\"","Damien looked offended. \"I’m early every day.\"","\"Yeah, yeah...\" Noah gave him a skeptical look. \"One minute before the first class starts. That’s your definition of early?\"","Damien laughed. \"But today I’m more than ten minutes early.\"","\"That’s actually unusual.\"","\"I woke up earlier than usual today.\" Damien stretched his arms behind his head before suddenly remembering something.","\"Oh, right. Master told me something yesterday.\"","\"Hmm?\"","Noah looked at him. \"What did Instructor Morgana tell you?\"","\"She didn’t tell me much.\"","Damien’s grin widened. \"She just said we’d get to hear something interesting tomorrow.\"","He shrugged.\"So let’s see what she has to say.\"","Noah’s curiosity immediately increased. \"Of course. Now I’m curious too.\"","\"Me too.\"","The two continued walking together. By the time they reached the classroom, several students were already inside.","The room was filled with the usual morning atmosphere.","Some students were chatting in small groups, while others were reviewing their notes. A few were leaning against their desks, talking about training from the previous day, while several students were still half-asleep and resting their heads on their arms.","The scrape of chairs against the floor mixed with the low hum of conversations.","Noah entered and immediately headed toward his usual seat. He chose the chair beside Lyria.","Damien sat beside him.","Lyria glanced at Noah with her beautiful pink eyes. For a brief moment, their eyes met. Then she quietly looked forward again.","Noah smiled faintly at her cute reaction.","The classroom gradually filled. One student after another entered until almost every seat was occupied.","The chatter continued for another minute.","The classroom door opened. Instructor Morgana walked inside.","The moment the students saw her, the noise began to die down.","Morgana walked to the front of the classroom with her usual calm expression and placed a few documents on the desk.","She looked across the room. \"Good morning, everyone.\"","\"\"\"Good morning, Instructor Morgana!!!\"\"\"","The students responded almost simultaneously.","Morgana nodded. \"Before we begin today’s lesson, I would like to make an announcement.\"","The remaining whispers immediately disappeared.","Several students straightened in their seats. An announcement from an instructor usually meant something important.","Morgana folded her hands in front of herself. \"It’s regarding your second unit test next month.\"","A few students immediately relaxed. \"Next month?\"","\"We still have plenty of time.\"","\"Wait, another test already?\"","Quiet murmurs spread through the classroom.","Morgana waited for a few seconds before continuing.","\"Yes. You still have plenty of time. The test will be held after the middle of next month.\"","Several students visibly relaxed.","\"However, I thought it would be better to inform you in advance so that you can prepare accordingly.\"","She paused.","\"And unlike the first semester, this examination will not involve a practical battle or a virtual reality match.\"","The classroom became noticeably quieter.","Morgana continued. \"This time, there will be a written examination only.\"","A collective groan immediately swept through the room. \"What?!\"","\"A written exam?\"","\"That’s worse!\"","\"I’d rather fight monsters!\"","A few students laughed, while others dramatically dropped their heads onto their desks.","Noah couldn’t help but smile.","Morgana remained completely unfazed.","\"Considering everything that has happened over the last few months, the academy has decided that it would be more appropriate to exercise greater caution.\"","She looked over the students.","\"So, for this particular examination, you will only need to study.\"","One student raised his fist.","\"That’s not comforting, Instructor!\"","A few students laughed again.","Morgana sighed lightly.","\"I was not finished.\"","The laughter immediately died down. \"But the more interesting announcement comes after that.\"","The students became attentive again.","Morgana picked up one of the documents from her desk.","\"After considerable discussion among the academy staff, we have decided to resume our usual field trips.\"","A wave of excitement immediately spread through the classroom.","\"Field trip?\"","\"Really?\"","\"Where are we going?\"","\"Please don’t tell me it’s dungeon!\"","\"Anywhere but a dungeon!\"","Morgana waited for the noise to settle before continuing.","\"This time, however, we have chosen a rather special destination.\"","The room gradually quieted.","\"Rather than visiting another location within the Aurellian Empire...\"","She paused deliberately.","\"...your next field trip will take you to another country.\"","The classroom exploded.","\"Another country?!\"","\"Seriously?!\"","\"Which one?\"","\"Is that even allowed?\"","Noah’s eyebrows rose. Even he hadn’t expected that.","Morgana finally revealed the destination.","\"The country we have selected is the Elven Kingdom of Elythraen.\"","A few students gasped. Others immediately began whispering excitedly among themselves.","\"The Elven Kingdom...\"","\"I’ve always wanted to see elven nation!\"","\"Do you think we’ll meet the royal family?\"","Morgana raised one hand, bringing the room back under control.","\"You will be visiting the capital city.\"","She spoke clearly.","\"Lunathiel.\"","The name alone caused another wave of excited murmurs. The capital of Elythraen. The heart of the elven kingdom. A place most students had only ever read about in history books.","Morgana continued.","\"And before anyone asks, yes, the Queen will be present in the capital during your visit.\"","The room became unusually quiet.","\"The Queen herself?\"","\"Well her home is there idiots.\"","\"So we can see world tree?!\"","Morgana gave them a small smile.","\"Naturally, the royal family will have strong security measures in place. You will not need to worry about your safety.\"","That was supposed to reassure them. Instead, the students became even more excited.","Noah, however, wasn’t excited at all. His expression had gone completely blank.","’Fuck this.’","His instincts were screaming at him.","’ Another incident is going to happen .’","He leaned back slightly in his chair and stared ahead.He had spent the past few weeks wondering when something troublesome would finally happen.","Now he had his answer.","’I actually thought the academy would avoid sending us anywhere outside the city after everything that happened. And no matter how much academy tries to keep students safe, it will be useless since that’s what story of game needed.’","And also now they weren’t merely leaving the city. They were leaving the empire.","And they were going straight to the capital of another kingdom.","Noah’s expression darkened.","One particular person immediately came to mind.","’Ken.’","His eyes narrowed.","’There’s no way this is a coincidence.’","Ken Takeane had already given Marina an Everbloom Draught. He had asked her to arrange a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And now, somehow, Noah’s class was being sent directly to Lunathiel.","’Ken knows something that going to happen.’","Noah’s fingers slowly tightened.","’Something is going to happen in Lunathiel.’","He stared at the front of the classroom while the excited voices of his classmates continued around him."]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: Maybe you don’t actually hate these rumors","paragraphs":["===STATUS===","Name: Lyria Sunweave","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 602","Speed: 597","Stamina: 599","Endurance: 590","Charm: 811","Mana: 6083","Core Rank: Condensed (Mid)","Potential: Sovereign Core (High)","Profession: [Spearmanship Lv.3], [Priestess Lv.3]","Technique: [Radiant Spear Art], [Mana Fist Art]","Affinity: Light","Spells: [Light Bullet],[Sphere of light], [Light Lance], [Heal], [Light Cannon], [Augmentation Buffer], [Cleansing Light], [Healing Touch], [Aegis of Light], [Flash Burst],[Light Prison]","Innate Ability: [Purification]","Passive Abilities: [Light of Hope], [Divine Resistance]","======","Classes had ended for the day.","Lyria walked through the academy corridors alongside Arisha and Emma, her footsteps quiet against the polished floor.","While the three girls made their way toward the dormitory area, Lyria’s attention was focused elsewhere. A translucent status window floated before her.","She quietly examined her current abilities and statistics, comparing them to what they had been before.","Her strength had increased. Her mana had grown considerably. Her techniques had improved.","’ I’m getting stronger...but still it’s slow compare to Noah or Damien... I need to work more hard!’","Lyria stared at her status but not for long.","\"I am really excited to visit the Elven Kingdom!\"","Emma’s cheerful voice pulled her out of her thoughts.","Lyria blinked and closed the status window.","Emma’s face was glowing with excitement. \"I’ve never been there before.\"","\"Neither have I,\" Arisha replied casually.","She walked between Emma and Lyria, her long violet hair swaying smoothly with every step.","\"This will be my first time as well.\"","Emma’s excitement grew even more. \"Hey, Lyria. What about you? Have you ever been to the Elven Kingdom?\"","Lyria nodded. \"Yes. I’ve been there a few times.\"","Her expression became slightly nostalgic. \"But the last time I visited was when I was twelve.\"","\"Oh!\"","Emma’s eyes widened. \"Were you there on vacation?\"","\"No.\" Lyria shook her head. \"My family is devoted to the Sun God, as you know. My father occasionally travels to the Elven Kingdom for religious visits.\"","\"Is that because of the World Tree?\"","\"Yes.\"","Lyria nodded.","\"The World Tree is said to contain the essence of prosperity and life. According to the legends, it protects the elves from many dangers.\"","Her voice became slightly softer as she explained. \"It is also said to have been a gift from the Sun God to the elves. And according to their beliefs, a deity of life resides within the tree—a daughter of the Sun God. So many consider the world tree as daughter of Sun God.\"","\"Wow~\"","Emma’s eyes sparkled. \"So the World Tree really has a deity living inside it?\"","\"That’s what the legends say.\" Lyria smiled faintly. \"Because of that, my family also visits the tree to pray whenever we travel there.\"","She paused. \"Unfortunately, I don’t remember much from my first visit. I was very young and didn’t even understand how to properly speak with others.\"","Emma chuckled. \"And you visited again when you were twelve?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"So it’s been quite a while since you’ve been there.\"","\"Indeed.\"","Lyria nodded.","\"Why didn’t you visit again?\" Arisha asked.","\"It was mostly because it wasn’t compulsory.\" Lyria shrugged slightly. \"My family considers the pilgrimage important, but I wasn’t required to accompany my father every time. After that, I became more focused on training and studying.\"","Arisha nodded in understanding. \"Then I’m more than ready to go.\"","She glanced ahead. \"And as for danger... well, we joined the academy to become stronger. We can’t spend our entire lives playing it safe.\"","\"I think the same!\" Emma enthusiastically bumped her fist into her palm.","\"Besides, we’re going to another country! How could I not be excited?\"","Lyria smiled at their enthusiasm. But their peaceful conversation was soon interrupted.","\"That’s Lyria, isn’t it?\"","A voice came from behind them. \"I heard she’s in a relationship with Noah.\"","\"What? Really?\"","\"I thought that was just a rumor.\"","The voices were quiet, but the academy corridor was relatively calm, allowing the words to reach Lyria’s ears clearly.","Her footsteps slowed. A faint blush immediately appeared across her cheeks.","Arisha noticed. \"Are you alright, Lyria?\" She glanced at her friend. \"Are those rumors bothering you?\"","\"No.\" Lyria quickly shook her head. \"They aren’t. I’m not worried about them at all.\"","Emma smiled. \"That’s good. Hopefully, the rumors haven’t reached your father yet.\"","Lyria smiled gently. \"It’s alright. In the end, they’re only rumors.\"","She wasn’t particularly worried. \"My father trusts me. Even if he heard them and had doubts, he would simply ask me about it, and I could tell him the truth.\"","Arisha suddenly gave her a teasing look. \"Hmm...\"","Lyria immediately became suspicious. \"What?\"","\"Maybe you don’t actually hate these rumors.\" Arisha’s lips curled into a mischievous smile. \"Perhaps you secretly like being called Noah’s lover.\"","\"What?!\" Lyria’s face instantly turned red.","\"Of course that’s not the case, Arisha!\"","She covered part of her burning face. \"You know that! Stop making fun of me!\"","Emma laughed. \"Yeah, there’s no way Lyria would actually like Noah.\"","Arisha raised one eyebrow. \"And why is that?\"","She looked at Lyria with an amused expression.","\"He’s the second-ranked student, talented, strong for his age, and considerably more handsome than he used to be. Not forgetting how many times he got in danger and survived them.\"","Lyria’s face became even redder.","Arisha continued mercilessly. \"He has also changed quite a lot since returning to the academy. And he has shown some interest in her several times.\"","\"W-Well...\" Lyria hesitated. \"I mean... you’re not wrong.\"","Emma’s eyebrows rose. \"Wait, you’re actually agreeing with her?\"","\"N-No! That’s not what I meant!\" Lyria hurriedly defended herself.","Arisha chuckled. \"There’s also the matter of Ophelia.\"","Lyria and Emma both looked at her. \"It seems the bitterness between her and Noah has decreased considerably. I’ve seen her talking to him and greeting him several times.\"","Arisha shrugged. \"Perhaps it’s because of her mother.\"","\"Now that you mention it...\" Emma placed a finger against her chin.","\"They don’t seem to be on bad terms anymore.\"","She glanced at Lyria. \"So maybe Noah isn’t such a bad choice for you.\"","\"H-Hey!\" Lyria’s face turned completely crimson. \"You two are going too far!\"","She finally raised her voice, clearly losing her patience with their constant teasing. \"Why are the two of you deciding things for me?!\"","Arisha and Emma exchanged amused glances. \"Hehe.\"","\"Lyria is cute when she’s flustered.\"","\"Very cute.\"","Neither girl showed any intention of stopping.","Lyria’s cheeks puffed slightly. Then she pointed a trembling finger directly at Arisha.","\"Y-You!\"","Arisha blinked innocently. \"He has shown more interest in you than he has in me!\"","Lyria’s accusation left Emma momentarily speechless.","Arisha, however, remained completely unfazed. She casually ran a hand through her long violet hair.","\"I don’t mind.\"","\"What?\"","\"If he wants to flirt with me, then he can.\" Arisha gave a small shrug. \"Perhaps he might even manage to win my heart.\"","Lyria’s pink eyes widened.","She had expected her words to embarrass Arisha or at least make her deny it. Instead, Arisha had calmly accepted the possibility.","Even Emma looked slightly surprised. Perhaps she was only teasing Lyria and deliberately turning the tables on her.","But judging by Arisha’s calm expression, it was impossible to tell.","Lyria stared at her for several seconds.","\"You... you are a terrible woman!\" She turned around and marched ahead.","\"Hey! Wait for us!\" Emma hurried after her.","\"Hey, Lyria! I’m sorry!\" Arisha followed as well, laughing softly.","The three girls continued down the corridor together, their voices gradually fading into the bustling academy halls."]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: What Should I do?","paragraphs":["\"What should I do?\"","Noah lay on his bed, staring at the ceiling as he thought about the danger that might be waiting ahead.","He had no solid evidence against Ken. The young man merely seemed suspicious because of the things he had done, particularly his strange interest in meeting the Elven Queen.","But could Noah actually confront him? Could he simply ask Ken whether he was a transmigrator?","There were too many possible outcomes.","Even if Noah confronted him and discovered that Ken really was a transmigrator with knowledge of the future, what were the chances that he would not be hostile?","What if Ken refused to cooperate with him? What if he saw Noah as a threat?","Worse, what if Ken deliberately fed him false information about the future and tried to manipulate him?","Noah himself was not a bad person, nor was he some ruthless villain.","However, he had read enough webnovels to know that transmigrated protagonists were not always kind-hearted heroes.","Many of them were villains or antiheroes—people willing to do morally questionable things, betray others, or even sacrifice innocent people if it meant surviving or achieving their goals.","To be honest, as a reader, Noah actually preferred those kinds of protagonists over the typical righteous heroes.","Villains and antiheroes were simply more interesting.","But now that he was actually living inside a game world, he desperately hoped that if Ken really was a transmigrator, he wasn’t some cold-blooded bastard who viewed everyone around him as disposable pawns.","’What a mess... Guess villains are only cool in novels, not in real life. Shit.’","There was also another possibility. Ken might not be a transmigrator at all.","Noah could simply be misunderstanding everything.","And if that was the case, confronting Ken would make things even more awkward. Noah could always dismiss his suspicions afterward, but what if Ken also had his own reasons for hiding certain things?","There was another problem.","If Ken really was a transmigrator, there was a good chance he had already realized that the current Noah was not the same person as the Noah from the original story.","After all, Noah’s personality had changed far too much.","If Ken knew the original story, he would probably have noticed it.","Noah cursed his luck.","He had been thrown into this world without any knowledge of what happened after the game’s original storyline.","He had no idea what the future held. He had no guide. Once again he felt useless.","With a tired sigh, Noah shook his head. For now, there was no reason to burden himself with endless possibilities.","The only thing he could do was observe. He shouldn’t act recklessly and expose his suspicions without enough evidence.","’I’ll just keep watching Ken for now.’","With that decision made, Noah closed his eyes.","He decided to sleep.","---","Next day.","\"Hello, Ken. We haven’t really talked much since the academy started.\"","Noah sat beside Ken during class while their instructor continued his lecture.","Today’s lesson was about monsters and beast-related knowledge.","Instructor Liam, an elderly man with a rather serious expression, stood at the front of the classroom. A large projection covered the wall behind him, displaying images of various Rank D and Rank C monsters while he explained their characteristics, habitats, and dangerous traits.","\"Yeah. Hello.\"","Ken replied casually, his dark-gray eyes remaining fixed on the projection. He was surprisingly attentive. He didn’t even glance at Noah.","’This guy... is really focused on studying.’","Noah also turned his attention toward the lesson. After a few seconds, however, he leaned slightly toward Ken.","\"By the way, are you excited about the field trip to the Elven Kingdom?\"","That finally made Ken turn toward him.","’Yeah! You must know I’m a transmigrator! Come on, Ken! Reveal yourself! Say that you need to tell me something important!’","\"Yes, actually. I’m quite excited.\"","Ken gave him a small smile. \"I’ve never been there before, so I think it will be an amazing experience.\"","With that, he turned his attention back toward the projection.","Noah’s lips twitched.","’Fair enough.’","He had to admit, Ken’s response was perfectly normal. There was nothing suspicious about it.","Noah leaned back in his chair and continued watching the lesson.","His thoughts briefly wandered toward his own abilities.","His sword technique, especially the one he used with his katana, allowed him to unleash an almost instantaneous slash.","The technique involved drawing the blade from its sheath and returning it before most people could even see the movement.","It was incredibly cool.","Noah couldn’t help but feel a little proud whenever he thought about it. Then, after a moment, another thought crossed his mind.","\"Hey...\"","Noah glanced at Ken.","\"I’ve mostly seen you together with Marina. Are you two dating or something?\"","Ken stiffened. It was subtle, but Noah noticed it immediately. The tips of Ken’s ears turned slightly red, and he quickly looked at Noah.","\"What are you saying?!\"","His usually calm expression was replaced by clear embarrassment. \"We’re just good friends! There’s nothing between us!\"","His voice rose slightly as he defended himself.","Noah raised an eyebrow. ’Oh? Interesting.’","Before he could ask anything else.","\"YOU TWO! STAND UP!\"","Both Noah and Ken flinched. They immediately stood from their seats. Instructor Liam glared at them from the front of the classroom, his expression darkening.","\"You two dare to chat during my class?!\"","He slammed his hand against the desk.","\"Now tell me! What was the sentence I spoke immediately before I caught you two talking?\"","Silence.","Noah and Ken looked at each other. Neither of them had the slightest idea.","\"...\"","\"...\"","Instructor Liam’s face twitched. \"You weren’t listening?!\"","He immediately launched into another furious lecture.","Meanwhile, Leonard, Damien, and Arisha watched the scene from their seats. Leonard was trying not to laugh.","Damien openly grinned. Even Arisha had a faint smile on her face as she watched Noah and Ken suffer under Instructor Liam’s wrath.","Noah could only sigh inwardly.","’Well... at least I learned one thing. Ken definitely doesn’t like being teased about Marina.’","But whether that meant anything more remained unknown."]}]);
